### Review API Tests with Image Upload

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@authToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjY4YTJkODYxMTdjOTNmYzI2OWRmNDEyMiIsInJvbGUiOiJ2ZW5kb3IiLCJpYXQiOjE3NTYwMTQ5NDAsImV4cCI6MTc1NjEwMTM0MH0.N_mKEo2K7i9h2Ru144X2Ef1C_GGBr_z20vKjfd_zsgI

@productId = 68a2d86117c93fc269df4122
@reviewId = 
@existingImages = ["https://example.com/image1.jpg", "https://example.com/image2.jpg"]

### 1. Create Review with Images
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

# Form data fields:
# - productId: {{productId}}
# - rating: 5
# - comment: This is an excellent product! Very satisfied with the quality.
# - images: [Select multiple image files - max 5 files, 5MB each]

###

### 2. Create Review without Images (Text only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

# Form data fields:
# - productId: {{productId}}
# - rating: 4
# - comment: Good product, would recommend to others.

###

### 3. Create Review with JSON (for testing without actual file upload)
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Amazing product! Love the quality and design. Fast delivery too!"
}

###

### 4. Get All Reviews for a Product (Admin Panel)
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/getAllReviews/{{productId}}?page=1&limit=10&sort=-createdAt
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 5. Get Product Page Reviews (User's review + other reviews)
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/productpage/{{productId}}?page=1&limit=5&sort=-createdAt
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 6. Update Review with New Images
PUT {{baseUrl}}/review/updateReview/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

# Form data fields:
# - rating: 4
# - comment: Updated review text with more details about the product.
# - existingImages: ["https://example.com/image1.jpg"] (JSON string of URLs to keep)
# - images: [Select new image files to add - max 5 files, 5MB each]

###

### 7. Update Review Text Only (No Images)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/review/updateReview/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

# Form data fields:
# - rating: 3
# - comment: Updated my rating after using the product for a month.
# - existingImages: [] (empty array to remove all existing images)

###

### 8. Update Review with JSON (for testing without file upload)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/review/updateReview/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "Updated review comment - product is good but could be better.",
  "existingImages": "[]"
}

###

### 9. Toggle Like on Review
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/Like/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 10. Delete Review (and associated images)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/review/deleteReview/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Error Cases

### 11. Create Review - Invalid Product ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "invalid-id",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "This should fail due to invalid product ID"
}

###

### 12. Create Review - Missing Rating
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "comment": "This should fail due to missing rating"
}

###

### 13. Create Review - Invalid Rating (out of range)
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "rating": 6,
  "comment": "This should fail due to invalid rating (> 5)"
}

###

### 14. Update Review - Non-existent Review ID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/review/updateReview/68a2d86117c93fc269df9999
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "This should fail - review not found"
}

###

### 15. Delete Review - Non-existent Review ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/review/deleteReview/68a2d86117c93fc269df9999
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 16. Access without Authentication
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/getAllReviews/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Pagination Tests

### 17. Get Reviews with Custom Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/getAllReviews/{{productId}}?page=2&limit=5&sort=rating
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 18. Get Reviews Sorted by Likes
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/productpage/{{productId}}?page=1&limit=10&sort=-likes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 19. Get Reviews Sorted by Date (Oldest First)
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/getAllReviews/{{productId}}?sort=createdAt
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Instructions for Testing with Images:
# 
# For requests with file uploads (multipart/form-data):
# 1. In VS Code REST Client, click "Send Request"
# 2. In the form that appears, fill in the text fields
# 3. For image fields, click "Choose File" and select image files
# 4. Supported formats: JPEG, PNG, WebP
# 5. Max file size: 5MB per image
# 6. Max files: 5 images per review
#
# For existingImages field in updates:
# - Send as JSON string: ["url1", "url2"] 
# - To keep specific images from previous upload
# - Send empty array [] to remove all existing images
#
# Variables to set:
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api (your server URL)
# @authToken = your_jwt_token_here
# @productId = valid_product_id_here  
# @reviewId = valid_review_id_here (get from create response)
